IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc23-transfers`

-- ccc23-tests-transfers.l4 -- tests for sections 672.86 to 672.95. Expected values are written from the text, never copied from the code.

§ `s 672.86`
-- (1) args: detained in custody or directed to attend at a hospital under a 672.54(c) or 672.58 disposition; (a) the Review Board of the province where the accused is detained recommends a transfer; (b) consent of the Attorney General of the receiving province; (b) consent of the Attorney General of the sending province
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an accused not so detained or directed: the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.86(1) the accused may be transferred to any other place in Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) args: an accused who is detained in custody is to be transferred
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2) an officer authorized by the Attorney General of the province where the accused is being detained must sign a warrant specifying the place in Canada to which the accused is to be transferred` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2) an officer authorized by the Attorney General of the province where the accused is being detained must sign a warrant specifying the place in Canada to which the accused is to be transferred` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2.1) args: not detained in custody; (a) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is being transferred recommends a transfer; (b) consent of the receiving Attorney General; (b) consent of the sending Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2.1) the accused who is not detained in custody may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2.1) the accused who is not detained in custody may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2.1) the accused who is not detained in custody may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2.1) the accused who is not detained in custody may be transferred to any other place in Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an accused who is detained in custody is outside (2.1)
#ASSERT `s 672.86(2.1) the accused who is not detained in custody may be transferred to any other place in Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) args: being transferred in accordance with (2.1); the order
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is being transferred must make the order` TRUE `s 672.86(3)(a) direct that the accused be taken into custody and transferred pursuant to a warrant under subsection 672.86(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is being transferred must make the order` TRUE `s 672.86(3)(b) direct that the accused attend at a specified place in Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is being transferred must make the order` FALSE `s 672.86(3)(a) direct that the accused be taken into custody and transferred pursuant to a warrant under subsection 672.86(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is being transferred must make the order` FALSE `s 672.86(3)(b) direct that the accused attend at a specified place in Canada` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(b) args: the order directs attendance at a specified place; the Review Board of the province to or from which the accused is being transferred considers the condition appropriate
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3)(b) the direction that the accused attend at a specified place is subject to the condition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3)(b) the direction that the accused attend at a specified place is subject to the condition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.86(3)(b) the direction that the accused attend at a specified place is subject to the condition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 672.87 to 672.89`
-- 672.87(a) args: a warrant described in 672.86(2); the person is responsible for the custody of the accused
#ASSERT `s 672.87(a) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person responsible for the custody of the accused to have the accused taken into custody and conveyed to the person in charge of the place specified in the warrant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.87(a) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person responsible for the custody of the accused to have the accused taken into custody and conveyed to the person in charge of the place specified in the warrant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.87(a) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person responsible for the custody of the accused to have the accused taken into custody and conveyed to the person in charge of the place specified in the warrant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.87(b) args: a warrant described in 672.86(2); the person is the person specified in the warrant; the detention is in accordance with a 672.54(c) disposition
#ASSERT `s 672.87(b) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person specified in the warrant to detain the accused` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.87(b) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person specified in the warrant to detain the accused` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.87(b) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person specified in the warrant to detain the accused` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.87(b) the warrant is sufficient authority for the person specified in the warrant to detain the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.88(1) args: the accused is transferred to the province under 672.86
#ASSERT `s 672.88(1) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred has exclusive jurisdiction over the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.88(1) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred has exclusive jurisdiction over the accused` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.88(1) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred may exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84 as if it had made the disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.88(1) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred must perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84 as if it had made the disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.88(1) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred may exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84 as if it had made the disposition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.88(1) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred must perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84 as if it had made the disposition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.88(2) args: transferred under 672.86; the agreement is subject to the Act
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Attorney General of the province to which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement with the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Attorney General of the province to which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement with the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Attorney General of the province to which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement with the Attorney General of the province from which the accused is transferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.88(2) the agreement's effect. args: an agreement is in force; the circumstances set out in it exist; its terms and conditions are met
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.88(2) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.89(1) args: detained in custody under a Review Board disposition; transferred to another province; the transfer is under 672.86
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred has exclusive jurisdiction over the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred has exclusive jurisdiction over the accused` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred has exclusive jurisdiction over the accused` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred has exclusive jurisdiction over the accused` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred may continue to exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred must continue to perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred may continue to exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred must continue to perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred may continue to exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred must continue to perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred may continue to exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(1) the Review Board of the province from which the accused is transferred must continue to perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.84` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 672.89(2) args: the accused is to be transferred as described in (1); the transfer has been made; the agreement is subject to the Act
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Attorneys General of the provinces to and from which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Attorneys General of the provinces to and from which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Attorneys General of the provinces to and from which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Attorneys General of the provinces to and from which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Attorneys General of the provinces to and from which the accused is transferred may enter into an agreement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.89(2) the agreement's effect. args: an agreement is in force; its circumstances exist; its terms and conditions are met
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.89(2) the Review Board of the province to which the accused is transferred exercises the powers and performs the duties referred to in subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 672.9 to 672.94`
-- 672.9 args: a warrant or process issued in relation to an assessment order or disposition; the place is in Canada outside the province where the order or disposition was made
#ASSERT `s 672.9 the warrant or process may be executed or served in the place as if it had been issued in that province` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.9 the warrant or process may be executed or served in the place as if it had been issued in that province` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.9 the warrant or process may be executed or served in the place as if it had been issued in that province` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.91 args: a peace officer (by s 2); the place is in Canada; grounds to believe that the accused has contravened; has wilfully failed to comply; is about to do so
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no reasonable grounds on any of the three: the text does not speak
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a peace officer, or "peace officer" not covered by section 2's list
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- outside Canada
#ASSERT `s 672.91 the peace officer may arrest the accused without a warrant` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.92(1) args: arrested under 672.91; subject to a 672.54(b) disposition or an assessment order; as soon as practicable; issues a summons or appearance notice; delivers the accused to the place specified
#ASSERT `s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.92(1) the peace officer may release the accused from custody, issue a summons or appearance notice and deliver the accused to the place specified` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.92(2) the bar. args: arrested under 672.91; subject to a 672.54(b) disposition or an assessment order; (a) belief that detention is necessary in the public interest; (b) belief that the accused is subject to an order of another province; (c) belief that the accused will fail to attend
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the three beliefs: the subsection does not bar, and the text does not say the release is allowed either
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- outside subsection (1)'s cases
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2) the peace officer is barred from releasing the accused under subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 672.92(2)(a): the four needs the circumstances include; any other need is not covered
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2)(a) the need is one of those that the circumstances include` `s 672.92(2)(a)(i) establish the identity of the accused` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2)(a) the need is one of those that the circumstances include` `s 672.92(2)(a)(ii) establish the terms and conditions of a disposition made under section 672.54 or of an assessment order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2)(a) the need is one of those that the circumstances include` `s 672.92(2)(a)(iii) prevent the commission of an offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2)(a) the need is one of those that the circumstances include` `s 672.92(2)(a)(iv) prevent the accused from contravening or failing to comply with the disposition or assessment order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(2)(a) the need is one of those that the circumstances include` `s 672.92(2)(a) another need` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) args: a peace officer does not release the accused
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused must be taken before a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the accused is arrested` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused must be taken before a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the accused is arrested` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) the time. args: the justice has jurisdiction in the territorial division of the arrest; without unreasonable delay; hours after the arrest
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE TRUE 24 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE TRUE 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE FALSE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(3) the accused has been taken before a justice in time` FALSE TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) args: arrested under 672.91; subject to a 672.54(c) disposition
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition must be taken before a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the accused is arrested` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition must be taken before a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the accused is arrested` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition must be taken before a justice having jurisdiction in the territorial division in which the accused is arrested` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) the time: same args as (3)'s time
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE TRUE 24 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE TRUE 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition has been taken before a justice in time` TRUE FALSE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(4) the accused subject to a paragraph 672.54(c) disposition has been taken before a justice in time` FALSE TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) args: a justice described in (3) or (4) is not available within twenty-four hours after the arrest
#ASSERT `s 672.92(5) the accused must be taken before a justice as soon as practicable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.92(5) the accused must be taken before a justice as soon as practicable` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 672.93(1) args: brought before the justice under 672.92; the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the accused has contravened or failed to comply
#ASSERT `s 672.93(1) the justice must release the accused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.93(1) the justice must release the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.93(1) the justice must release the accused` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.93(1) the justice must release the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1.1) args: the justice releases the accused
#ASSERT `s 672.93(1.1) notice must be given to the court or Review Board that made the disposition or assessment order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.93(1.1) notice must be given to the court or Review Board that made the disposition or assessment order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) args: the justice is satisfied of reasonable grounds; the order is made pending a hearing; the order is appropriate in the circumstances; the order is that the accused be returned to a place specified
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) the justice may make the order in relation to the accused` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "including" an order that the accused be returned to a specified place: within the power without a separate finding of appropriateness
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) the justice may make the order in relation to the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) the justice may make the order in relation to the accused` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) the justice may make the order in relation to the accused` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) the justice may make the order in relation to the accused` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) the notice. args: the justice makes an order under (2)
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) notice must be given to the court or Review Board that made the disposition or assessment order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.93(2) notice must be given to the court or Review Board that made the disposition or assessment order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 672.94 args: the Review Board receives a notice given under 672.93(1.1) or (2)
#ASSERT `s 672.94 the Review Board may exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.83 as if it were reviewing a disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.94 the Review Board must perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.83 as if it were reviewing a disposition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 672.94 the Review Board may exercise the powers mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.83 as if it were reviewing a disposition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 672.94 the Review Board must perform the duties mentioned in sections 672.5 and 672.81 to 672.83 as if it were reviewing a disposition` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
